Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:08:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test queue watch newest mtime and inclusive granule
 boundary

Close #2675 mutation gaps with public changed() behavior on real temporary DB/WAL files and a controlled integer clock. Both file orders preserve same-stamp wakeups; exact-granule age owes a recheck while granule+1 settles. No production change.

Proof: focused canonical suite 13 passed, 0 skipped with file retries disabled. max-to-min mutant: 2 failed/11 passed; <=-to-< mutant: 1 failed/12 passed; restored suite 13 passed. Equality is reachable under time.time_ns and stat integer timestamps, so the boundary mutant is non-equivalent.
